# Agent Knowledge System

This directory is the entry point for coding agents working in
`/Users/jinleic/jinleic-workspace`. It separates stable policy, current facts,
procedures, evidence, memories, and archives so agents do not treat every
Markdown file as equally authoritative.

## Authority model

Use local material in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md` (core rules plus a routing table; source `AGENT_POLICY.md`)
   and the equally binding topic files in `md_files/` it routes to, for stable safety,
   placement, and routing policy.
2. `CURRENT_FACTS.md` for locally verified paths and runtime mappings.
3. Routed workflows under `dotfiles/codex/prompts/` for operational procedure.
4. Active project files for project-specific state and completion gates.
5. `runbooks/` for reusable procedures and prior verified techniques.
6. `data/`, dated archives, and `archive/` (retired files) for evidence and history only.
7. Claude or Codex memory for discovery context, never as unverified live truth.

Higher-priority system, developer, tool, and direct user instructions still win
over every workspace document.

## Start here

| Need | Read first |
|---|---|
| Workspace rules: core policy and topic routing table | `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md`; topic files in `../../md_files/` |
| Topic or artifact discovery | `CATALOG.md` |
| Current local mappings | `CURRENT_FACTS.md` |
| Skill selection | `SKILLS.md` |
| Independent model delegation (models: `DELEGATE_MODELS.json`) | `MODEL_DELEGATION.md` |
| Document status and placement | `DOCUMENT_LIFECYCLE.md` |
| Cleanup state and rollback hashes | `CLEANUP_PLAN.md` |
| Acceptance and regression evidence | `VALIDATION.md` |
| Local cleanup decisions and recovery | `LOCAL_CLEANUP_DECISIONS.md` |
| Retired files: ledger and restore commands | `../../archive/MANIFEST.md` |
| General inference runbooks | `../../runbooks/README.md` |
| K8s reproduction snapshot | `../../k8s-set-up-runbooks/README.md` |
| Abandoned research institute (2026-09-20); historical evidence only | `../../research-institute/README.md` |
| Archived mathematics trees (distinct `math` and `maths`) | `../../research-institute/math/README.md`, `../../research-institute/maths/README.md` |
| Archived physics open-problem research | `../../research-institute/physics/README.md` |
| Archived theoretical CS open-problem research | `../../research-institute/cs/README.md` |
| Workspace root registry (classification) | `PROJECTS.json` |
| Campaign lifecycle + compact per-target state | `../../scripts/campaign.py` |

## Retrieval rules

- Use targeted `rg` searches from workspace root. The root `.ignore` removes
  archives, telemetry, raw exports, dependencies, temporary `scratch/`
  experiments, immutable source-snapshot payloads, and known sensitive material
  from default search. Transaction READMEs and manifests remain searchable.
- Use `rg --no-ignore` only when the task explicitly needs historical or raw
  evidence.
- Do not search `ssh-sync/` as a knowledge source.
- Do not open secret-bearing files merely to decide whether they are relevant.
  Use path-only scans and approved secret retrieval mechanisms.
- Prefer one canonical document over repeated export-pack copies.

## Maintenance rules

- Keep the root instruction files below 200 lines and 12 KB each.
- Generate inventories; do not paste full file lists into always-loaded policy.
- Every operational document promoted as current should declare `status`,
  `owner`, and `last_verified` or `snapshot_date`.
- Reclassify stale material instead of silently treating it as current.
- Do not delete or disable anything without explicit user approval.
