STATUS.md:38:| Li Jin-Hua, Lou Sen-Yue, "Kac–Moody–Virasoro symmetry algebra of a (2+1)-dimensional bilinear system", *Chin. Phys. B* **17**(3), 747–753 (2008), doi:[10.1088/1674-1056/17/3/002](https://doi.org/10.1088/1674-1056/17/3/002) | Book's Ref. [6]. Three explicit models: (i) `D_y D_x D_t F·G = 0, D_x D_t F·G = 0` (bilinear form of the isotropic integrable sine-Gordon / Loewner–Konopelchenko–Rogers system); (ii) `(D_t + D_x^2)F·G = 0, D_y(D_t + D_x^2)F·G = 0` (a subcase of the bilinear non-isotropic sine/sinh-Gordon system); (iii) `(D_t + D_x^3)F·G = 0, D_y(D_t + D_x^3)F·G = 0`, shown to have infinitely many generalized symmetries (formal series symmetry approach) and a Kac–Moody–Virasoro point-symmetry algebra. Asks (their Eq. (7)) whether `(D_t + D_x^n)F·G = 0, D_y(D_t + D_x^n)F·G = 0` is integrable for other n, and states the ansatz (62)–(63). | Full text read: CPB site PDF (`https://cpb.iphy.ac.cn/en/article/pdf/preview/10.1088/1674-1056/17/3/002.pdf`, sha256 `9186c7bf…a739d`) |
